                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is mildly decreased (62 mL/min/1.73 m²), indicating stage 2 chronic kidney disease. This is common in elderly patients and may reflect age-related decline. Regular monitoring of renal function and assessment for risk factors or progression is recommended. No acute abnormality detected.</td>
